No construction may be initiated within the City of Danielsville for any residential building of any type which:

- 1. Employs a gravity tank-type, flushometer-valve, or flushometer-tank toilet that uses more than an average of 1.6 gallons of water per flush; provided.

- 2. Employs a shower head that allows a flow of more than an average of 2.5 gallons of water per minute at sixty (60) pounds per square inch of pressure;

- 3. Employs a urinal that uses more than an average of 1.0 gallons of water per flush;

- 4. Employs a lavatory faucet or lavatory replacement aerator that allows a flow of more than 2.0 gallons of water per minute; or

- 5. Employs a kitchen faucet or kitchen replacement aerator that allows a flow of more than 2.5 gallons of water per minute.
